---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const allPosts = await getCollection('blog', ({ data, id }) => !data.draft && !id.endsWith('.draft.md'));
const allPostsData = allPosts.map((p) => ({
  slug: p.id,
  title: p.data.title,
  description: p.data.description,
  tags: p.data.tags,
}));

const rules = [
  {
    title: 'Stick to the MVP',
    body: 'With yourself as the client it is too easy to widen the scope mid-build. I listed the site structure, wrote down every element each page needed, and held the line.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Avoid trends',
    body: 'I deliberately stayed off other personal sites while building. Influence is easy to absorb without noticing, and six months later you want to tear the whole thing down.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Build it fast',
    body: 'Momentum is what stops you backing out or changing your mind. I set a realistic schedule and kept to it. Shipping something imperfect beats not shipping.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Make it personal',
    body: 'The most important rule. The point was to do it my own way and say who I am, not to impress anyone in particular.',
  },
];

const design = [
  {
    label: 'Layout',
    value: 'A sticky left rail carries identity and a numbered index; everything else is one reading column.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Type',
    value: 'Three roles, strictly kept: Source Serif 4 for display, Inter for prose, JetBrains Mono for metadata and code.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Colour',
    value: 'Warm paper and ink with a single cobalt accent. Dark mode is warm graphite, never blue-black.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Depth',
    value: 'No drop shadows outside the search overlay. Hairlines, inset fills, and a 2px accent bar do the work.',
  },
];

const stack = [
  { label: 'Framework', value: 'Astro', link: 'https://astro.build' },
  { label: 'Styling', value: 'Tailwind CSS', link: 'https://tailwindcss.com' },
  { label: 'Content', value: 'Markdown content collections' },
  { label: 'Fonts', value: 'Source Serif 4, Inter, JetBrains Mono' },
  { label: 'Syntax highlighting', value: 'Shiki (github-light / github-dark)' },
  { label: 'Analytics', value: 'Cloudflare Web Analytics', link: 'https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/' },
  { label: 'Webmention', value: 'Webmention', link: 'https://www.w3.org/TR/webmention/' },
  { label: 'Hosting', value: 'GitHub Pages' },
  { label: 'CI / CD', value: 'GitHub Actions' },
  { label: 'Package manager', value: 'Bun' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Colophon | Amaan Ul Haq Siddiqui"
  description="How this site was built and the thinking behind it."
  allPosts={allPostsData}
>
  <div class="stack">
    <header>
      <h1 class="page-title">Colophon</h1>
      <p class="page-lede" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        A colophon is a short note about how something was made. In books it sits at the back,
        a quiet record of the decisions that shaped the final object. This is mine.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- ── 01 Approach ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="idx">01</span>
        <h2>Approach</h2>
        <span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <p class="entry-summary">
          You are no doubt familiar with the old adage: the toughest client is yourself. It is
          true, and designing your own site is a frustrating experience because of it.
        </p>
        <p class="entry-summary" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
          Every personal project I had taken on before turned into a messy, drawn-out,
          indecisive process. I would struggle to produce anything I liked, change my mind every
          five minutes, and lose interest. To stop that happening again I set myself four rules.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 02 The rules ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="idx">02</span>
        <h2>The rules</h2>
        <span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      <ol class="rules">
        {rules.map((rule, i) => (
          <li class="panel">
            <span class="rule-n">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <p class="entry-name">{rule.title}</p>
              <p class="entry-summary" style="margin-top:0.4rem">{rule.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <p class="meta" style="margin-top:1rem;padding-left:0.85rem">
        Four rules made every later decision simpler.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 03 Design ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="idx">03</span>
        <h2>Design</h2>
        <span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="panel panel-flush">
        {design.map((item) => (
          <div class="defrow">
            <span class="dt">{item.label}</span>
            <span class="dd">{item.value}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 04 Why Astro ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="idx">04</span>
        <h2>Why Astro</h2>
        <span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <p class="entry-summary">
          Astro gets out of the way. It builds plain static output that deploys to GitHub Pages
          behind a small CI workflow: no server to manage, nothing to keep patched. For a personal
          site that combination is hard to beat.
        </p>
        <p class="entry-summary" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
          It also gets the defaults right. Zero JavaScript ships unless you opt in, content
          collections validate frontmatter against a schema at build time, and the component model
          is there in full when a page actually needs it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 05 Built with ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="idx">05</span>
        <h2>Built with</h2>
        <span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="panel panel-flush">
        {stack.map((item) => (
          <div class="defrow">
            <span class="dt">{item.label}</span>
            <span class="dd">
              {item.link ? (
                <a href={item.link} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link">{item.value}</a>
              ) : (
                item.value
              )}
            </span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Source ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section>
      <div class="panel panel-quiet">
        <p class="entry-summary">
          The source is open at{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/amaanx86/amaanx86.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link">github.com/amaanx86/amaanx86.github.io</a>.
          Traffic goes through Cloudflare Web Analytics, which sets no cookies, and Webmention
          carries replies and references from other sites back here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
